  "assessments": [
    {
      "item": "model and contract",
      "judgment": "Original String ownership is preserved independently from parsed/final URL. Invalid URL versus supported-scheme rejection, HTTP2xx/non2xx, Request actual error and Timeout remain distinct. Headers-only boundary is accurate: response status/final URL copied then response dropped, no body-read await, no false claim that transport received zero bytes. Option<u128> None denotes no request attempt, Some(0) is possible; std elapsed measures only real attempt, not paused Tokio10seconds. Debug-only derives avoid needing equality on error payloads."
    },
    {
      "item": "completion logic",
      "judgment": "Client has limited5 redirects/direct choice with no explicit reqwest request deadline. Parse rejects before Instant/timeout. Work async block contains GET/send factory and wait, so single Tokio timeout covers redirect to final headers; pinned cooperative timeout limitation is preserved. Nested results handled without? because every attempted record returns Check; reqwest is_timeout maps separately. Successful HTTP200/404/500 and loop6hits/redirect2hits align with previously reviewed API/source."
    },
    {
      "item": "source and manifests",
      "judgment": "B1 starter is honest fixed incomplete Scheme marker; standalone copied manifest literal fields and absolute adjustment of dev path dependency are explicitly taught before Cargo. Checks directory is not auto-target, full cfg(test) module appends exactly once. Complete tests exactly equal checks suffix. Local-service normal lib and its http-single dependency config/error/reply complete sources are all inline; no dependency examples/binary/integration/cfg(test) code is compiled by selected B1 test/example. Seven normal dependency files match own sealed14 source hashes."
    },
    {
      "item": "tests, lifetimes and cleanup",
      "judgment": "All six finite tests/helpers are visible. Check fields/reqwestError are Send; owned client/original in spawned async block do not borrow Fixture. held_request has real5second entered observation and on mismatch abort+await request before server shutdown. Timeout test waits true entered before pause, then20second borrowed&mutJoinHandle guard; resume occurs on every returned route before cleanup. Successful output is not awaited twice; guard expiry still aborts+awaits original handle. Under pinned Tokio JoinHandle is Unpin+Future, matching borrowed wait syntax taught before first timeout-test snippet. Invalid/scheme/work/request/timeout distinctions and output-time assertions use match/None appropriately. Missing work timer remains finitely observable rather than hanging test."
    },
